{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1145735-what-arcana-would-be-needed-for-a-tripwire-spell","id":1145735,"title":"What Arcana would be needed for a tripwire spell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-01T02:02:16-07:00","id":1145735,"title":"What Arcana would be needed for a tripwire spell","content":"Just a quick question.<br /> <br /> What Arcana would you need for a spell that creates a magical &quot;trip wire&quot; that lets the Mage know every time another supernatural crosses it. E.G. you think you've cornered something in a house so you put a tripwire around it encase it sneaks past you and escapes - or it's friends come to help.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing Space 2 Prime 1?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T05:21:44-07:00","id":1145763,"title":"","content":"Prime 1 is enough, it's just a Prime version of &quot;Web of Life&quot;. However, as Prime is not really the arcanum of the supernatural, but rather that of the supernal, it's supernatural detection prowesses are a bit blunted (though still existent, see &quot;Supernal Vision&quot;). At base such a spell would enable you to sense all Mages/Sleepwalkers/Sleepers in an area and when one enters or leaves the area. A vampire walking in would not trigger it at all (which of course in itself can arouse suspicion, but that's not what you're looking for). A reach, similar to the one in &quot;Supernal Vision&quot; however could include supernatural creatures not connected to the supernal. Keep in mind that they would only ping as a vague something, unless you mix in the appropriate Arcana. A mage who casts this spell with the reach option would be informed the man in front of his is some kind of supernatural and that there are two others in his room, but unless he also mixes in Death and Spirit, which would tell him that this man is a ghoul and that there is a Ghost and Spirit in this room, presumably in twlight, he would remain clueless as to their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T06:18:43-07:00","id":1145773,"title":"","content":"That seems clear cut <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T06:30:33-07:00","id":1145777,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d also allow Space to alert you when anything moves past a defined border, and it could probably give you a brief vision of the interloper.<br /> <br /> Basically, a Space version of Fate\u2019s Oaths Fulfilled (Though it only works for this specific purpose) which also functions well for the purpose of acting as a tripwire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T00:12:45-07:00","id":1150276,"title":"","content":"How does distance work here with such a spell? If I put a magical alarm system up and then leave my house, does the spell still reach me with its alarm despite any distance or do I need to expand the Area scale for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T01:39:57-07:00","id":1150283,"title":"","content":"Normally, you would feel the &quot;ping&quot; no matter how far, Scale in this cases usually measures the area protected or covered by the intrusion alarm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: you could limit it to the same world, though. If you have the alarm set in the physical realm and it triggers while you are in, say, the Shadow, you might not sense it until you return to the world of flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-17-2017, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T04:06:11-07:00","id":1150296,"title":"","content":"No, crossing realm barriers doesn\u2019t stop your already cast magic from functioning unless that realm has characteristics that do specifically that. So if you set up a tripwire spell in the material and then went to the Shadow you\u2019d still get the alert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}